<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacobite rising of 1745</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1745">1745</a>–<a href="/years/1746">1746</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Forty-five, Jacobite rebellion of 1745</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jacobite rising of 1745 was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-edward-stuart">Charles Edward Stuart</a>'s attempt to regain the British thrones for his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-francis-edward-stuart">James Francis Edward Stuart</a>. Landing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>, won at Prestonpans and marched as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derby">Derby</a> before retreating. The Jacobite army was destroyed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-culloden">Culloden</a> in April 1746, after which the Highlands were harshly repressed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1745.jpg" alt="Jacobite rising of 1745" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Morier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Culloden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
